From: Strata maintainers <noreply@lgse.com>
Subject: [PATCH] a11y: express widget bounds from the parent border origin

GtkWidget's bounds relative to its parent use the parent's content coordinate
space. AT-SPI composes the result as though it used the parent's border origin,
losing the parent's padding and border. Translate the bounds before exposing
them through GtkAccessible.

This test-image-only patch is licensed under LGPL-2.1-or-later, matching
gtk/gtkwidget.c.
---
 gtk/gtkwidget.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gtk/gtkwidget.c b/gtk/gtkwidget.c
index d71b480d26..a80be006d1 100644
--- a/gtk/gtkwidget.c
+++ b/gtk/gtkwidget.c
@@ -8861,6 +8861,17 @@ gtk_widget_accessible_get_bounds (GtkAccessible *self,
     }
   else
     {
+      if (parent != NULL)
+        {
+          graphene_rect_t parent_bounds;
+
+          if (gtk_widget_compute_bounds (parent, parent, &parent_bounds))
+            {
+              bounds.origin.x -= parent_bounds.origin.x;
+              bounds.origin.y -= parent_bounds.origin.y;
+            }
+        }
+
       *x = floorf (graphene_rect_get_x (&bounds));
       *y = floorf (graphene_rect_get_y (&bounds));
       *width = ceil (*x + graphene_rect_get_width (&bounds)) - *x;
--
2.51.0
